My DeepSeek (dsh-plugin-my-deepseek)
====================================

Bundled upstream work
---------------------
This package bundles the official DeepSeek chat demo front end:

  deepseek-ai/chat-demo
  Licensed under the MIT License — the complete text ships in vendor/LICENSE.

Modifications to that source fall into two groups: changes generated by the
build scripts, and changes written by hand.

### Generated by scripts/ (re-applied automatically on every build)

  - design tokens are renamed from --dsw-* / --ds-* into a private --dsc-*
    namespace, and the dark-mode flag becomes body[data-dsc-dark], so the panel
    keeps the official palette without redefining the harness theme's tokens;
  - the same dark-mode flag is renamed in app/theme.ts, which is the code that
    sets the attribute: the stylesheet and the code that toggles it must agree on
    the name or dark mode silently never applies;
  - page-level body rules from global.css are scoped to .dsc-root;
  - the sidebar title renders the official wordmark instead of the demo's own
    "API usage demo" label.

### Written by hand (must be re-applied when the vendored demo is upgraded)

Import-path rewrites. Relative import specifiers cannot be redirected by a
bundler alias, so these are plain source edits. Targets are written with the
extension the source file actually has:

  services/chat/db.ts                       -> web/src/shared/store-api.ts
  components/sider/Sider.tsx                -> web/src/shared/brand-wordmark.tsx
  services/api/client.ts                    -> web/src/shared/api-auth.ts
  services/chat/store.ts                    -> web/src/shared/model.ts
                                             -> web/src/shared/compact-history.ts
                                             -> web/src/shared/fork.ts
  components/settings/SettingsDialog.tsx    -> web/src/components/AccountField.tsx
                                             -> web/src/shared/save-file.ts
  components/settings/settingsDialogState.ts -> web/src/shared/account.ts
  components/chatInput/ChatInput.tsx        -> web/src/shared/account.ts

Feature seams added to the demo. Each is a small insertion that calls into our
own modules; keeping the demo's structure intact is what makes upstream
upgrades tractable:

  services/api/client.ts
    account-authenticated requests are delegated to the native shell; error
    handling only treats 401 as a dead account token when that shell carried
    the credential. Requests that pass an explicit API key are never delegated.

  services/chat/store.ts
    model selection reads a single source instead of a constant;
    the request history is projected through the compaction layer;
    forking a conversation into a new session.

  services/chat/types.ts
    a session carries optional fork lineage, stripped on export.

  services/api/types.ts
    the model identifier is a plain string, so a model the server adds does not
    require a client change.

  services/settings.ts
    a compaction preference; settings persistence is disabled in the memory-only
    build.

  components/settings/SettingsDialog.tsx
    renders the account sign-in row, the compaction selector and the version
    row at the bottom of the general section; the history export hands the
    archive to the shell, because a WebView does not act on blob: download links.

  components/settings/Settings.module.css
    one `.descriptionLink` class so an inline link inside a row description keeps
    the demo's own type scale and palette instead of the browser default.

  components/settings/settingsDialogState.ts
    a signed-in account counts as usable credentials.

  services/chat/db.ts
    attachment originals stay in memory in the memory-only build instead of
    being written to IndexedDB.

  components/messages/{UserMessage,AssistantMessage}.tsx, components/base/icons.tsx
    the branch-from-here action and its icon.

  components/chatInput/ChatInput.tsx
    the attachment entry is disabled when only an account token is available,
    because the upload endpoint requires an API key.

  app/App.tsx
    the credential check waits for the account restore to settle, so a signed-in
    account does not trigger the "no API key" prompt on every cold start.

  i18n/{zh,en}.ts
    strings for the additions above.

  env.d.ts
    the memory-only build constant.

Modified upstream files (total): 17 · Re-applied by hand on upgrade: 17 (all of
the above) · Generated by scripts/: the token, scoping and wordmark changes.

